**Experiment 126 summary**: RWKV-style token shift for attention K/V inputs. Before computing keys and values, each token's representation is mixed with the previous token's via learnable per-channel sigmoid gates. Q is unshifted. This gives K/V projections access to local bigram context before attention computes it — a simplified form of RWKV-6 time mixing, which is explicitly listed as a priority-1 architectural direction. Adds only 8192 params (0.01%), zero crash risk.
